   "file": "Collectors.dc.html",
   "title": "Collectors \u00b7 list, add, Folder collector",
   "heading": "Collectors \u00b7 built-in Folder",
   "intro": "Collectors fill the queue on a schedule: <b>Folder</b> (built in) or a <b>custom script</b>. The detail answers one question at a glance, \u201cis it working, and what did it last do?\u201d: a status card, a compact read-only settings block (Edit turns it into a form in place), and the last three runs. Healthy rows in the list have no pill; only Running, Failed and Needs your OK do. Adding is three short steps with defaults (Folder: <code>~/Distill Inbox</code>, Keep the original, every hour, the active vault). Folder copies by default and remembers what it took (by content), shown as the <b>Already collected</b> link with Forget. It also collects Google Docs (.gdoc) and, with <b>Include subfolders</b> (on by default), each subfolder as one folder item.",
