   "file": "CollectorsScript.dc.html",
   "title": "Collectors \u00b7 custom script (consent, schedule, run log)",
   "heading": "Collectors \u00b7 custom script",
   "intro": "Same layout as Folder. Setup is two sheet steps (script, then schedule), then the new collector asks once before it ever runs: <b>\u201cDistill will run this code on your Mac as you\u201d</b>, with the code shown. The allowance is tied to the script\u2019s sha256, so a changed script pauses and asks again. At a glance: status card, settings (script, schedule, allowed), and the last runs; interpreter, timeout, cron and the arguments it gets ($1/$2, DISTILL_VAULT, DISTILL_QUEUE_DIR) sit under <b>Advanced</b>. Output shows only in an opened run, or live while it runs.",
