  {
   "file": "CollectorsScriptFiles.dc.html",
   "title": "Collectors \u00b7 script files, packages and Run now",
   "heading": "Collectors \u00b7 script files, packages, Run now",
   "intro": "A script Distill keeps is now <b>a real file</b>, not code inside collectors.json: each collector gets its own folder (<code>~/Library/Application Support/Distill/collectors/scripts/&lt;id&gt;/</code>) with <code>collector.zsh</code>, <code>.py</code>, <code>.js</code> or <code>.ts</code>, so it can be found, edited in any editor, backed up and versioned. <b>Reveal in Finder</b> and <b>Open in editor</b> sit next to it. Languages: zsh, Python, JavaScript and TypeScript (run on your Node with the types stripped). <b>Packages</b>: package.json (npm, into node_modules/) for JavaScript and TypeScript, requirements.txt (pip, into .venv/) for Python, all inside that folder. Your OK covers the script and its manifest, so a changed package list asks first, like a changed script. <b>Packages install when you allow the script</b> (adding it, or after a manifest change), so a collector is ready before its first run; a run started during an install waits for it. <b>Run now</b> is in the same place for every collector and state (Stop while running, Allow and run while it needs your OK), first in every \u22ef menu, and always on the selected list row. A manual run shows its result and last output lines in the status card at once. <b>Test run</b> (scripts only, a quiet link before Run now) runs it exactly the same way but into Distill\u2019s test folder, so trying an edit never feeds the next batch. Your own file still works: Distill runs it where it is.",
